# Customize: what the selected row does (2026-11)
help.section.appearance = Theme, colours, size and transparency of the interface.
help.section.layout = The picker's shape and place, and what it shows around the inputs.
help.section.inputs = Which inputs show, their names, icons and order.
help.section.previews = A picture of each source on its tile.
help.section.clock = A clock on screen while the picker is open.
help.section.remote = The keys that open this picker, and its delays.
help.section.avr = Control a Denon or Marantz receiver over the network.
help.section.general = Language, the Customize tile, updates and reset.
help.language = Language of the interface. Automatic follows the TV's.
help.show_customize_tile = Shows the Customize tile after the inputs. Hidden, the arrow that moves nothing in the picker still opens this menu.
help.theme = Colours of the panel, the tiles and the text.
help.accent = Colour of the selection and of what is active.
help.corners = Shape of the panel's and the tiles' corners.
help.size = Size of the whole interface, to set for your distance from the screen.
help.show_panel = Background behind the tiles. Off, the tiles sit directly on the picture.
help.opacity = The lower the value, the more the picture shows through the panel.
help.dim = Darkens the picture around the panel while it is open.
help.animations = Fades and glides on opening and while moving.
help.layout = The picker's shape: row, grid, list or sidebar. OK shows all four.
help.position = Where on screen the panel appears. OK places it on a preview of the screen.
help.show_icons = Shows an icon on each input.
help.show_header = Shows the title and the input being watched at the top of the picker.
help.show_hints = Shows the key reminders at the bottom of the picker.
help.show_disconnected = Also shows HDMI inputs with nothing plugged in.
help.show_devices = Shows the detected device and its port under the input's name.
help.show_live_tv = Shows Live TV (antenna, cable, satellite) among the inputs.
help.naming = How inputs are named: after the device plugged in, or the label set in the TV.
help.show_previews = Shows on each tile a picture of what the source is playing.
help.preview_fps = How often the live preview refreshes. Higher rates ask more of the TV.
help.capture_access = Lets Outpick capture the TV's picture: on this model the previews need it.
help.show_home = Shows a tile that goes back to the TV's home screen.
help.show_usb = Shows USB sticks and drives plugged in.
help.show_media_servers = Shows media servers (DLNA) found on the network.
help.auto_close = Closes the picker after this long without a key press.
help.clock_show = Shows the time on screen while the picker is open.
help.clock_style = The clock's look.
help.clock_size = The clock's size.
help.clock_24h = Hours from 0 to 23. Off: from 1 to 12.
help.clock_seconds = Shows the seconds too.
help.clock_place = Moves the clock with the arrows, anywhere on screen.
help.source_key = The remote's Source (Input) key opens this picker instead of LG's.
help.switch_delay = Source pressed again in the picker: the next input is taken after this delay.
help.multikey_opens = A short press on Multikey (···) opens this picker. A long press stays LG's accessibility menu.
help.sources = For each input: show or hide it, choose its icon, rename it, move it.
help.reset = Restores the original appearance, layout and clock. Inputs, remote, receiver and language are kept.
help.avr_enabled = Adds to the receiver's input options its own inputs, its volume, its sound mode and its setup menu.
help.avr_device = The receiver to control: found automatically, picked from the list, or given by its IP address.
help.avr_protocol = How to talk to the receiver. Leave it on Automatic unless it does not answer.
settings.long_press = Long press time
settings.hold_gap = Arrow repeat gap
value.ms = {n} ms
help.long_press = How long OK or Back is held for its long press (options, close everything). Raise it if long presses fire by accident.
help.hold_gap = The same arrow again faster than this is held: it stops at list ends and opens nothing. Raise it if a held arrow still wraps around, lower it if quick presses count as held.

